{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"smallest"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"tolerance"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1e-8, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"maxIterations"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":"? = nil) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/Eigenpairs","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Eigenpairs","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory10EigenpairsV"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"parameters":[{"name":"smallest","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The number of eigenpairs, in ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"name":"tolerance","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The residual a Ritz pair must reach, relative as described above."}]}]},{"name":"maxIterations","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for the limits"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"under Throws."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component by component: each component’s null vector first (eigenvalue 0, components in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of their least vertex), then the smallest positive eigenvalues of the components"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"merged. On a component of at least 64 vertices, thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reorthogonalization and locking, the null vector projected out, from a fixed start vector:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on σI − M (σ Gershgorin’s bound) while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on M⁺ by shift-invert, each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"product a conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair is accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ, relative to itself as for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"algebraicConnectivity"},{"type":"text","text":"; the vectors found are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value is its vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The dense solver on a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"component, or when k is a third of it or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}]},{"name":"Precondition","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"text":" is in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when given, is at least 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run by shift-invert spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1,000 when nil), or a conjugate-gradient solve inside it 20,000 + 2n iterations, without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging. A run on σI − M hands over to shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n products or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", whichever is smaller. The dense solver throws as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"laplacianSpectrum"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/normalizedLaplacianEigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxIterations:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/normalizedlaplacianeigenpairs(smallest:tolerance:maxiterations:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","title":"normalizedLaplaci